From: Grische <2787581+grische@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Apr 2026 15:16:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] batadv: fix mesh-vpn interface name comparison

strcmp only compared the first strlen(ifname) characters, so any interface
with a prefix of "mesh-vpn" (e.g. "mesh") incorrectly matched.

Using sizeof("mesh-vpn")<IF_NAMESIZE as the bound to include the null
terminator in the comparison, ensuring an exact match without assuming
ifname is null-terminated.

(cherry picked from commit f291cb04b2232e1358b92d7b392bf97ae5413cec)
---
 src/batadv.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/batadv.c b/src/batadv.c
index 0ca83dc..2e3a858 100644
--- a/src/batadv.c
+++ b/src/batadv.c
@@ -96,7 +96,7 @@ static int parse_orig_list_netlink_cb(struct nl_msg *msg, void *arg)
 		return NL_OK;
 
 	opts->stats->neighbor_count++;
-	if (!strncmp(ifname, "mesh-vpn", strlen(ifname))) {
+	if (!strncmp(ifname, "mesh-vpn", sizeof("mesh-vpn"))) {
 		opts->stats->vpn.tq = nla_get_u8(attrs[BATADV_ATTR_TQ]);
 		opts->stats->vpn.connected = 1;
 	}
